    "description": "* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is expected.\n\n* WHERE...Maricopa County in south central Arizona...\n\n* WHEN...Until 200 PM MST Saturday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flooding of the Salt River below Granite Reef Dam is\nimminent or occurring. Flooding of low water crossings across the\nSalt River upstream of Tempe Town Lake, including McKellips Road,\nis imminent or occurring.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 517 AM MST, SRP was releasing 1650 cfs from Granite Reef Dam.\nFlooding is ongoing or expected to begin shortly.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nSalt River between Granite Reef Dam and Tempe Town Lake.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood",
